    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d281-a1">

                <pb facs="0345" n="331" xml:id="pg331"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 1]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Statement by General McCoy</hi>
                </head>
                <p>The members of the Commission will recall that paragraph 16 <hi
                        rendition="#italic">c</hi>, FEC–032/26,
                    “Interim Import-Export Policies for Japan”, adopted by the Commission on July
                    24, 1947, provided for the use of certain Japanese-owned stocks of precious
                    metals and stones, for acquiring foreign exchange to assist in financing a
                    portion of the Japanese trade program. The Supreme Commander has now forwarded
                    to the Commission Circular No. 9, which has been issued to implement the
                    Commission’s policy statement. This Circular, together with an explanatory
                    statement thereof, has been circulated as MI-. … The Supreme Commander is about
                    to take such steps as are necessary for the accomplishment of this program, and
                    I am therefore calling it to the attention of the Commission at this time.</p>
            </div>
